// Generated by `make -C js/i18n` from src/help.en.md. Edit the Markdown, not this file.
export default {
  "intro": "",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "help-basics",
      "nav": "Basics",
      "html": "<p>Type a calculation on any line and its result appears right beside it as a dimmed hint. Errors show inline in red. The <strong>total</strong> at the bottom sums all numeric results — use its dropdown to switch to the <strong>average</strong> or <strong>median</strong> — and results are formatted with thousands separators. Results show up to 3 decimal places (<strong>Settings → Decimal precision</strong>); a value with more precision ends with an ellipsis, while calculations keep full precision.</p>\n<p>The footer&#39;s <strong>−</strong> / <strong>+</strong> change the editor text size (50–200%, with <strong>Reset size</strong> back to 100%). On a first visit a <strong>Welcome</strong> sheet demonstrates the app; use its <strong>Keep content</strong> / <strong>Clear content</strong> buttons to dismiss or empty it. As you type, a popup suggests variables, <strong>#tags</strong> and built-in names (or press <strong>Ctrl+Space</strong>): <strong>↑</strong>/<strong>↓</strong> to choose, <strong>Enter</strong>/<strong>Tab</strong> to insert, <strong>Esc</strong> to dismiss.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"1 + 1\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 2</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"2 * 3 + 1\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 7</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"(4 / 2) ^ 2\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 4</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"sqrt(16)\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 4</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"10 % 3\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 1</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"1000000\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 1,000,000</span></div><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operator</th>\n<th>Function</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>+</code></td>\n<td>Add</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>-</code></td>\n<td>Subtract</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>*</code></td>\n<td>Multiply</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>/</code></td>\n<td>Divide</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>^</code></td>\n<td>Power</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>%</code></td>\n<td>Remainder</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Many more functions and operators are available — see the <a href=\"https://mathjs.org/docs/expressions/syntax.html#operators\">mathjs documentation</a>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-tabs",
      "nav": "Tabs",
      "html": "<p>Use the tabs at the top to keep separate worksheets. Every tab is saved automatically as you type.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Switch</strong> — click a tab (or use <code>←</code>/<code>→</code> once focused, or <code>Ctrl+Tab</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Reorder</strong> — click and drag a tab to a new position.</li>\n<li><strong>Rename</strong> — double-click the tab name.</li>\n<li><strong>Close</strong> — click the <code>×</code> (you&#39;ll be asked to confirm).</li>\n<li><strong>Add</strong> — click the <code>+</code> tab.</li>\n<li><strong>Export / Import</strong> — use the buttons in the <strong>Settings</strong> modal to download the active sheet as text or load one from a file.</li>\n<li><strong>Share</strong> — the <strong>Share</strong> button copies a link that carries the active sheet inside it. Anyone who opens it is asked whether to open the sheet in a new tab; it never replaces what they already have. Nothing is uploaded: the sheet travels in the link&#39;s <code>#</code> fragment, which browsers never send to a server.</li>\n</ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-comments-labels-tags",
      "nav": "Comments, labels & tags",
      "html": "<p>Everything after a <code>#</code> followed by a space is ignored (a comment). A <code>label:</code> before an expression names the line without being evaluated.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"2 + 2 # this is a note\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 4</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"Price: 10 + 5\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 15</span></div><p>With no space, <code>#word</code> is a <strong>tag</strong>. A line that is only tags shows their total, and <code>sum</code>/<code>total</code>/<code>average</code>/<code>avg</code> (optionally <code>of</code>) before the tag also work. Tagged lines above are summed, wherever they are. A row with several tags is the full amount split equally between them, so each tag gets its share while the row and its group total keep the full price. Tags can also be used in calculations: <code>#food * 2</code>, <code>#food + #other</code>. Requesting a tag that has no tagged lines shows an error.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"20 #food\n30 #food\n#food\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">last line returns 50</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"20 #food\n30 #food\n#food * 2\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">last line returns 100</span></div><p><strong>Tip:</strong> click a line&#39;s number in the left gutter to comment or uncomment that line — handy for switching a calculation off without deleting it. A line that already starts with <code>##</code> just loses one <code>#</code>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-variables",
      "nav": "Variables",
      "html": "<p>Assign a value with <code>=</code> and reuse it on later lines. Use <code>prev</code> for the most recent result above — it skips comments and blank lines. <code>sum</code>/<code>total</code>/<code>average</code>/<code>avg</code> aggregate the lines above until a blank line, which starts a new block.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"pizzas = 2\npizzaPrice = 30\npeople = 4\n(pizzas * pizzaPrice) / people\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">last line returns 15</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"20\nprev * 4\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">last line returns 80</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"10\n# a comment in between\nprev + 1\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">last line returns 11</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"10\n20\nsum\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">last line returns 30</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"4\n8\naverage\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">last line returns 6</span></div><p>Objects group named values; reach a field with a dot.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"invoice = {subtotal: 120, tax: 12}\ninvoice.subtotal + invoice.tax\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">last line returns 132</span></div><p>Variable names can contain spaces.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"monthly rent = 1500\nmonthly rent * 12\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">last line returns 18,000</span></div><p>Reference the result of a line above with <code>line(n)</code>. The reference shows the value inline (the raw <code>line(n)</code> stays visible while you edit that line) and only lines above can be referenced.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"5\nline(1) * 2\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">last line returns 10</span></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-groups",
      "nav": "Groups",
      "html": "<p>Open a named group with a label on its own line (like <code>Groceries:</code>) and close it with <code>end</code>. The header shows the group&#39;s subtotal and the whole group is shaded as a box; the inner lines still count in the bottom total. Blank lines inside are ignored, and <code>sum</code>/<code>average</code> inside a group total that group. A header with no <code>end</code> is just a label, and an <code>end</code> with no header is an error.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"Groceries:\n4.50\n3.20\n2.40\nend\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">header shows 10.1</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"Trip:\n10 cm\n1 m\nend\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">header shows 1.1 m</span></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-functions",
      "nav": "Functions",
      "html": "<p>Store a function with <code>f(x) = …</code> and call it later. Numi-style aliases are available too: <code>ln</code>, <code>fact</code>, <code>arcsin</code>, <code>arccos</code>, <code>arctan</code>, <code>root</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"double = f(x) = x * 2\ndouble(21)\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">last line returns 42</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"fact(5)\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 120</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"ln(e)\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 1</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"root(8, 3)\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 2</span></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-lists",
      "nav": "Lists",
      "html": "<p>Write a list with square brackets. Lists are <strong>1-indexed</strong>: <code>n[1]</code> is the first element. Slice with a range, assign elements, do element-wise arithmetic, and combine lists with the mathjs functions. Lists are capped at 100 items.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"[1, 2, 3]\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">[1, 2, 3]</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"n = [10, 20, 30]\nn[1]\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">10 (first element)</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"n = [10, 20, 30, 40]\nn[2:4]\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">[20, 30, 40]</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"n = [10, 20, 30]\nn[2] = 99\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">sets the second element</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"[1, 2] + [3, 4]\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">[4, 6]</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"expenses = [1200, 80, 45]\nsum(expenses)\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">last line returns 1325</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"mean(1:10)\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 5.5</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"sort([3, 1, 2])\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">[1, 2, 3]</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"concat([1, 2], [3, 4])\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">[1, 2, 3, 4]</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"m = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]\nm[2, 1]\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">3</span></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-sequences-iteration",
      "nav": "Sequences & iteration",
      "html": "<p>A range <code>start:end</code> (with an optional <code>:step</code>) makes a list of numbers, and calling a function with a range applies it to every element. Lists can be named and indexed like any other variable. Ranges are capped at 100 items.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"1:5\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"1:2:10\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">[1, 3, 5, 7, 9]</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"n = 1:5\nn[3]\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">3</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"double = f(x) = x * 2\ndouble(1:5)\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">[2, 4, 6, 8, 10]</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"sum(1:100)\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 5050</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"mean(1:5)\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 3</span></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-percentages",
      "nav": "Percentages",
      "html": "<p>Use <code>of</code>, <code>on</code> and <code>off</code> with <code>%</code> for percentage math.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"20% of 10\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 2</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"5% on 30\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 31.5</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"6% off 40\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 37.6</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"50 as a % of 100\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 50</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"5% of what is 6\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 120</span></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-rounding",
      "nav": "Rounding",
      "html": "<p>Round a result with a phrase at the end of the line, or call <code>round</code>, <code>ceil</code> or <code>floor</code> directly. Rounding works with units and currencies too.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"1/3 to 2 dp\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 0.33</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"π to 5 digits\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 3.14159</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"5.5 rounded\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 6</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"5.5 rounded up\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 6</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"5.5 rounded down\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 5</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"37 to nearest 10\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 40</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"$490 rounded to nearest hundred\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns US$ 500</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"21 rounded up to nearest 5\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 25</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"0.534 to nearest 16th\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 9/16</span></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-operators-scales",
      "nav": "Operators & scales",
      "html": "<p>Word operators and number scales work naturally: <code>plus</code>, <code>minus</code>, <code>times</code>, <code>multiplied by</code>, <code>divided by</code>, <code>with</code>, <code>without</code> and <code>mul</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"8 times 9\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 72</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"2 plus 3\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 5</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"10 minus 3\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 7</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"6 multiplied by 7\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 42</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"10 divided by 2\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 5</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"2 hours with 30 minutes\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 150 minutes</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"2 hours without 30 minutes\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 90 minutes</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"3 mul 4\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 12</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"2k\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 2,000</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"1kk\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 1,000,000</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"1kkk\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 1,000,000,000</span></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-unit-conversion",
      "nav": "Unit conversion",
      "html": "<p>Convert units with <code>to</code>, <code>in</code> or <code>as</code>. CSS units are supported too: <code>px</code>, <code>em</code> and <code>point</code>. Cooking volume units follow the measurement system in <strong>Settings → Measurement system</strong> — Metric (default), US customary or Imperial — which sets <code>cup</code> (250 / 236.6 / 284.1 ml), <code>tsp</code>, <code>tbsp</code>, <code>fl oz</code>, <code>pint</code>, <code>quart</code> and <code>gallon</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"1cm to m\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 0.01 m</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"2h to s\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 7200 s</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"5km to m\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 5000 m</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"30 degC to degF\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 86 degF</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"100 lb in kg\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 45.36 kg</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"1 cm in px\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns ≈ 37.8 px</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"2 em in px\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">returns 32 px</span></div><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Base</th>\n<th>Unit</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Length</td>\n<td>meter (m), inch (in), foot (ft), yard (yd), mile (mi), link (li), rod (rd), chain (ch), angstrom, mil</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Surface area</td>\n<td>m2, sqin, sqft, sqyd, sqmi, sqrd, sqch, sqmil, acre, hectare</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Volume</td>\n<td>m3, litre (l, L, lt, liter), cc, cuin, cuft, cuyd, teaspoon, tablespoon</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Liquid volume</td>\n<td>minim (min), fluiddram (fldr), fluidounce (floz), gill (gi), cup (cp), pint (pt), quart (qt), gallon (gal), beerbarrel (bbl), oilbarrel (obl), hogshead, drop (gtt)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Angles</td>\n<td>rad (radian), deg (degree), grad (gradian), cycle, arcsec (arcsecond), arcmin (arcminute)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Time</td>\n<td>second (s, secs, seconds), minute (mins, minutes), hour (h, hr, hrs, hours), day (days), week (weeks), month (months), year (years), decade (decades), century (centuries), millennium (millennia)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Frequency</td>\n<td>hertz (Hz)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Mass</td>\n<td>gram(g), tonne, ton, grain (gr), dram (dr), ounce (oz), poundmass (lbm, lb, lbs), hundredweight (cwt), stick, stone</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Electric current</td>\n<td>ampere (A)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Temperature</td>\n<td>kelvin (K), celsius (degC), fahrenheit (degF), rankine (degR)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Amount of substance</td>\n<td>mole (mol)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Luminous intensity</td>\n<td>candela (cd)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Force</td>\n<td>newton (N), dyne (dyn), poundforce (lbf), kip</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Energy</td>\n<td>joule (J), erg, Wh, BTU, electronvolt (eV)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Power</td>\n<td>watt (W), hp</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pressure</td>\n<td>Pa, psi, atm, torr, bar, mmHg, mmH2O, cmH2O</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Electricity and magnetism</td>\n<td>ampere (A), coulomb (C), watt (W), volt (V), ohm, farad (F), weber (Wb), tesla (T), henry (H), siemens (S), electronvolt (eV)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Binary</td>\n<td>bits (b), bytes (B)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>See the <a href=\"https://mathjs.org/docs/datatypes/units.html#reference\">mathjs units reference</a> for the full list.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-cooking-measures",
      "nav": "Cooking & measures",
      "html": "<p>Convert between dimensions by naming what you are measuring. The subject is free-form and optional: a known ingredient uses its density, a fuel its energy density, media their bitrate, and anything else a default (water). Write it before <code>to</code>/<code>in</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"300g butter in cups\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">≈ 1.32 cups</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"2 cups flour in grams\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">265 grams</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"1 cup sugar in grams\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">211.25 grams</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"300g in cups\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">1.2 cups (subject optional)</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"300g feathers in cups\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">1.2 cups (any subject works)</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"1 l petrol in kWh\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">9.5 kWh</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"2 hours 4k video in GB\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">14.4 GB</span></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-rates",
      "nav": "Rates",
      "html": "<p>A rate is one unit per another. mathjs does the arithmetic; these phrases make rates easy to write.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"90 km / 3 day\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">30 km/day</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"30 hours at 10 km/hour\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">300 km</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"100 km at 10 km/hour\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">10 hours</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"24 km a day for a year\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">8,766 km</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"time to upload 3 GB at 10 MB/s\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">300 s</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"5 km in 25 min\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">05:00/km</span></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-currency-conversion",
      "nav": "Currency conversion",
      "html": "<p>Convert between currencies using 3-letter ISO codes or symbols. Results are written with the currency&#39;s symbol where it has one (<code>350usd</code> becomes <code>US$ 350</code>); currencies without a symbol keep their code. Money only forms ratios (<code>USD/hour</code>, <code>USD/km</code>), so multiplying a currency by another unit (<code>BRL hour</code>) is an error — use a rate instead. Rates come from the European Central Bank (via frankfurter.dev) and are cached locally for offline use.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"100 USD to EUR\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">converts USD to EUR</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"$5 to GBP\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">converts to GBP</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"R$5 to EUR\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">converts to EUR</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"50 EUR in BRL\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">converts to BRL</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"100 USD/hour\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">US$ 100 per hour</span></div><p><strong>Supported codes:</strong> <code>AUD</code>, <code>BRL</code>, <code>CAD</code>, <code>CHF</code>, <code>CNY</code>, <code>CZK</code>, <code>DKK</code>, <code>EUR</code>, <code>GBP</code>, <code>HKD</code>, <code>HUF</code>, <code>IDR</code>, <code>ILS</code>, <code>INR</code>, <code>ISK</code>, <code>JPY</code>, <code>KRW</code>, <code>MXN</code>, <code>MYR</code>, <code>NOK</code>, <code>NZD</code>, <code>PHP</code>, <code>PLN</code>, <code>RON</code>, <code>SEK</code>, <code>SGD</code>, <code>THB</code>, <code>TRY</code>, <code>USD</code>, <code>ZAR</code>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-dates",
      "nav": "Dates",
      "html": "<p>Convert unix timestamps with <code>fromunix</code>, get the current time with <code>unix()</code>, and use date units directly.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"fromunix(0)\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">Jan 1, 1970…</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"fromunix(1446587186)\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">Nov 3, 2015…</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"unix()\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">current timestamp</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"1 month in days\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">30.4375 days</span></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-calendar",
      "nav": "Calendar",
      "html": "<p>Add or subtract time from a date, measure the interval between dates, and format a date with a pattern. Dates can be written as <code>10 June</code>, <code>June 10, 2023</code>, <code>2019-04-01</code> or <code>12/02/1988</code>. A date can be saved in a variable and reused (<code>start = March 4</code>, then <code>start + 2 weeks</code>). Clock times (<code>9:45 am</code>, <code>1:30</code>) add durations and measure intervals, shown in 24-hour by default (<strong>Settings → Clock</strong>). Workdays are Monday to Friday (public holidays are not counted yet).</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"10 June + 3 weeks\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">1 July</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"start = March 4, 2025\nstart + 2 weeks\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">18 March 2025</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"April 1, 2019 - 3 months 5 days\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">27 December 2018</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"3 weeks after March 14, 2019\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">4 April 2019</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"today + 3 weeks\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">three weeks from today</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"4 days from now\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">four days from now</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"16:00 + 3 hours 12 minutes\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">a clock time 3¼ hours later</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"7:30am to 8:45pm\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">13 hours 15 minutes</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"now + 3 hours 15 minutes\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">a clock time 3¼ hours from now</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"January 10 - February 5\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">3 weeks 5 days</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"days until Christmas\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">days until 25 December</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"workdays in 3 weeks\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">15 workdays</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"work hours in June\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">176 work hours (8h days)</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"10 March to 17 March in workdays\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">5 workdays</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"5 workdays after March 14, 2019\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">21 March 2019</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"weekday on March 9, 2024\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">Saturday</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"March 12, 2023 as EEEE, MMM d, yyyy\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">Sunday, Mar 12, 2023</span></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-timespans",
      "nav": "Timespans",
      "html": "<p>Show a duration as a timespan of components, or split it into two units. A timespan is a real duration, so it can be added and multiplied, and converted to a single unit with <code>to</code>/<code>in</code>/<code>as</code> (<code>as minutes</code>). Time units can be written short (<code>3h 5m 10s</code>) or long.</p>\n<div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"5.5 minutes as timespan\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">5 min 30 s</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"4.54 hours as timespan\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">4 hours 32 minutes 24 seconds</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"72 days as timespan\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">10 weeks 2 days</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"3h 5m 10s\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">3 hours 5 minutes 10 seconds</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"3h 5m 10s in seconds\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">11,110 seconds</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"12.5 minutes in minutes and seconds\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">12 min 30 s</span></div><div class=\"help-example\" data-expr=\"5.5 minutes as timespan\nline(1) + 1h\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\"><code></code><span class=\"help-returns\">last line: 1 hour 5 minutes 30 seconds</span></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-shortcuts-files",
      "nav": "Shortcuts & files",
      "html": "<p>The active sheet can be exported and imported from the <strong>Settings</strong> modal or with the shortcuts below.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Shortcut</th>\n<th>Action</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>⌘Z</code> <code>Ctrl+Z</code></td>\n<td>Undo the last change in the tab</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>⇧⌘Z</code> <code>Ctrl+Shift+Z</code></td>\n<td>Redo</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Ctrl+Tab</code> <code>Ctrl+⇧Tab</code></td>\n<td>Next / previous tab</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>⌘1…9</code> <code>Ctrl+1…9</code></td>\n<td>Jump to the nth tab</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>⌘F</code> <code>Ctrl+F</code></td>\n<td>Find &amp; replace in the active sheet</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>⌘G</code> <code>Ctrl+G</code></td>\n<td>Jump to a line number</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Tab</code></td>\n<td>Indent the line or selection</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>⇧Tab</code></td>\n<td>Outdent the line or selection</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>⇧⌘C</code> <code>Ctrl+Shift+C</code></td>\n<td>Copy the current line&#39;s result</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>⇧⌘S</code> <code>⇧⌘L</code></td>\n<td>Copy a share link for the active sheet</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>⇧⌘E</code> <code>Ctrl+Shift+E</code></td>\n<td>Export the active sheet</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>⇧⌘I</code> <code>Ctrl+Shift+I</code></td>\n<td>Import a sheet</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>⇧⌘⌫</code> <code>Ctrl+Shift+Backspace</code></td>\n<td>Clear the active sheet</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"
    },
    {
      "id": "help-about",
      "nav": "About",
      "html": "<p>Math Notes is a browser-based inline calculator, inspired by <a href=\"https://numi.app\">Numi</a> and <a href=\"https://soulver.app\">Soulver</a>. Its source is open — see the <a href=\"https://github.com/imaginamundo/math-notes\">GitHub repository</a>.</p>\n<p>Calculations run on <a href=\"https://mathjs.org\">mathjs</a>, an extensible math library for JavaScript, and currency conversion rates come from the <a href=\"https://www.ecb.europa.eu\">European Central Bank</a> via <a href=\"https://frankfurter.dev\">Frankfurter</a>.</p>\n<p>Your sheets stay on your device: they are saved in your browser&#39;s storage and are never sent to a server.</p>"
    }
  ]
};
